lesson(4,"Companies: governance, benefits and limits","distinguish ownership from management and evaluate benefits alongside governance costs",
 "separate legal identity, shares and continuity","capital structure and the consequences of financing decisions",
 "Shareholders hold ownership interests, while directors oversee a company and managers carry out delegated operations. Their roles can overlap but are not identical. Pooling equity can support expansion, while administration, reporting and conflicts of interest create costs. A private-company model restricts transfers or access to investors; a company offering securities to the public faces additional applicable requirements. Public offering is not the same as government ownership, and not every company is stock-exchange listed. Actual OHADA forms must be checked rather than importing foreign membership limits.",
 "A fictional company’s managers propose buying machinery. Owners may expect returns, while directors must assess risks and oversight. A declared dividend can be allocated among identical shares, but owning shares does not guarantee a dividend every year. The illustration does not identify any real Cameroonian firm’s current ownership or performance.",
 "Ask who owns, who supervises and who manages. Explain a potential benefit and its condition rather than asserting that incorporation automatically improves performance. Use only a dividend explicitly declared in the question; do not turn a model return into an investment promise.",[
 F("shareholder","a holder of an ownership interest","A person owns shares without running daily production.","Every shareholder is automatically the daily production manager.","Ownership and daily management can be separated."),
 F("director oversight","supervision and strategic responsibility through the company’s governing structure","The board questions a machinery proposal and monitors management.","Delegating daily work removes every need for oversight.","Delegation still needs accountability and supervision."),
 F("dividend","a distribution to shareholders when validly declared under the applicable conditions","The model allocates a declared payment across identical shares.","Shares guarantee a fixed dividend every year regardless of conditions.","A dividend is not an unconditional fixed debt payment."),
 F("governance cost","resources needed for administration, oversight and accountability","The company spends time preparing records and reporting decisions.","Company administration never uses scarce resources.","Oversight and compliance require time and resources even when useful.")],dividend,prereq=[3])

