choose=qa(5,"compare",2,[item("In an invented case, "+description+". Which form most directly matches the stated priority?",name,[(other,"That form emphasises a different ownership/control arrangement; compare the stated priority rather than the firm’s size.") for other,d in CHOICES if other!=name],"The priority described is "+description+"; no form guarantees success.") for name,description in CHOICES])
lesson(5,"Guided comparison of business units","choose a defensible form for a fictional case and explain a trade-off rather than naming a universal winner",
 "sole ownership, partnerships and company identity","cooperative study and the later locality business-planning case",
 "This guided classroom comparison applies the earlier lessons. Ownership, liability, finance, control and continuity are separate criteria. The best fit depends on the case’s priorities and constraints, not the biggest-sounding name. A form can solve one problem while creating another: pooled funds may require shared control, and liability protection can involve greater formality. A cooperative is introduced here as member-owned and democratically controlled; later lessons examine it more fully. No actual business is registered in this exercise.",
 "Fictional cases compare a Buea repair stall, a Bamenda workshop with complementary partners, a Douala company seeking equity and a group of growers seeking shared services. The same commercial activity can use different legal forms. Learners should read the ownership and purpose described rather than decide that all farms or shops have one form.",
 "Make a comparison sheet with ownership, decision method, finance and an important limitation. State a choice, cite a case fact and acknowledge a cost. If legal feasibility or actual demand is unknown, list what needs checking instead of inventing a guarantee.",[
 F("ownership criterion","identifying who holds the business interests","The comparison asks whether one person or a group owns the enterprise.","An employee count alone establishes ownership.","Staff numbers and ownership are separate features."),
 F("finance criterion","examining where funds can come from and on what terms","A case considers owners’ contributions alongside borrowing.","The legal form guarantees unlimited free finance.","Funding still depends on resources, terms and willingness to contribute."),
 F("control criterion","examining who makes decisions and is accountable","Learners compare sole control with shared or democratic decisions.","Every form gives one manager unlimited personal ownership rights.","Control arrangements differ and must be read from the form and case."),
 F("reasoned trade-off","a choice supported by a benefit and a recognised limitation","A pupil supports shared ownership for pooled skills while noting possible conflict.","A justified answer must claim that its preferred form has no drawback.","A reasoned comparison can favour an option while recognising its costs.")],choose,prereq=[1,2,3,4])

