lesson(6,"Capital structure of companies","distinguish equity from debt and relate nominal issued, called and paid-up capital in a stated textbook model",
 "shares, shareholder returns and company financing needs","the practical calculation of capital amounts",
 "Capital structure describes the financing mix, especially equity and longer-term debt. Equity includes owners’ funds and retained earnings; debt requires repayment under agreed terms. In the stated school share-capital model, authorised capital is the permitted nominal ceiling, issued capital the nominal value allocated, called capital the amount requested on issued shares, and paid-up capital the amount actually received. These are distinct from a share’s market price. Legal terminology and permitted payment schedules vary; the model does not announce an OHADA filing rule or minimum capital.",
 "An invented company may issue nominal shares but request only a stated instalment. If some called funds are unpaid, paid-up capital is below called capital. It may also borrow or retain earnings; neither is another issue of shares. Ordinary shares carry a residual ownership claim; preference shares have stated preferential rights. A debenture is a debt instrument. Reserve capital in some textbook treatments is uncalled capital reserved for a specified event, not retained-profit reserves.",
 "Label the quantity, value per share and stage first. In a consistent instalment example, authorised ≥ issued ≥ called ≥ paid-up nominal amounts. Check unpaid calls separately. Debt interest, preferred distributions and ordinary dividends have different terms; no payment is risk-free merely because the example names it.",[
 F("equity finance","owners’ financing interests, including retained earnings","The company keeps some profits rather than distributing them.","Retained earnings are automatically a new bank loan.","Retaining profit is internal equity financing, not borrowing."),
 F("debt finance","borrowed funds repayable under agreed terms","A lender provides funds with a stated repayment obligation.","A loan always gives the lender an identical ordinary-share ownership interest.","A debt claim differs from an ordinary equity interest."),
 F("called capital","the amount requested on issued shares in the stated instalment model","The company requests part of the nominal amount allocated.","Calling an amount proves every holder has already paid it.","A request creates called capital; receipts determine paid-up capital."),
 F("paid-up capital","the called share-capital amount actually received in the model","Some holders have paid, while another called amount remains unpaid.","Paid-up capital includes all amounts merely authorised but never issued.","Only actual received share-capital contributions enter paid-up capital here.")],issued,
 worked({},"A model issues {50} shares of nominal {1000} CFA francs, calls {600} per share and has unpaid calls of {2000}. Find issued, called and paid-up capital.",["Issued: {50} × {1000} = {50*1000}.","Called: {50} × {600} = {50*600}.","Paid-up: {50*600} − {2000} = {50*600-2000}."],"Issued {50*1000}; called {50*600}; paid-up {50*600-2000} CFA francs."),prereq=[3,4])

CAPV={"a":{"int":[6,12]},"b":{"int":[2,5]},"issued":{"expr":"b*10"},"authorised":{"expr":"a*10"},"nominal":1000,"called":{"pick":[400,600,800]},"unpaidShares":{"int":[1,5]},"calledTotal":{"expr":"issued*called"},"arrears":{"expr":"unpaidShares*called"},"paid":{"expr":"calledTotal-arrears"}}
def capital_record():
    """An SVG table whose displayed amounts are computed at render time."""
    parts=[json.dumps('<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 280" role="img" aria-label="Classroom capital reconciliation table in CFA francs"><rect width="320" height="280" rx="8" fill="#f3f2ed"/><g fill="#243c30" font-family="sans-serif" font-size="14"><text x="12" y="24">CFA francs - classroom model</text>')]
    for i,(label,expr) in enumerate([("Authorised ceiling","80*1000"),("Issued nominal","50*1000"),("Called","50*600"),("Paid-up","50*600-2000"),("Uncalled on issue","50*(1000-600)"),("Arrears","2000")]):
        y=56+i*35
        parts += [json.dumps(f'<text x="12" y="{y}">{label}</text><text x="307" y="{y}" text-anchor="end">'),"fmt("+expr+")",json.dumps('</text>')]
    parts.append(json.dumps('</g></svg>'))
    return "+".join(parts)
