lesson(7,"Practical preparation: capital calculations","calculate authorised, issued, called, paid-up and uncalled amounts from a labelled fictional record",
 "the company-capital distinctions just learned","judging financing constraints and later growth plans",
 "This practical uses a simplified classroom record, not an actual share issue. Start by labelling authorised and issued share counts, nominal value, the call per share and unpaid calls. Multiply a share count by a per-share amount to obtain capital in CFA francs. Called but unpaid is arrears; issued but not yet called is uncalled. Unissued shares are neither called nor paid-up capital. A diagram of gaps or a table can help keep these distinctions visible.",
 "Record these model columns in an exercise book: share count, nominal value, amount called and amount received. For issued shares, split nominal capital into called and uncalled; split called into paid-up and arrears. The same money must not be added twice. The displayed table matches the worked example and helps check the stages before independent questions.",
 "Check units and identities: issued = called + uncalled; called = paid-up + arrears. Authorised minus issued is the unissued ceiling. These equalities concern the stated instalment model; they are not a balance-sheet total including debt or profit reserves. Correct a heading error before doing arithmetic.",[
 F("nominal issue","issued share count multiplied by nominal value","A pupil multiplies allocated shares by their face value.","Issued capital is always the number of shares without a currency unit.","Multiplying by currency per share produces a capital amount."),
 F("arrears","called share contributions not yet received","The model records a requested amount that remains unpaid.","Arrears mean an amount that has never been called.","Arrears were requested; uncalled capital was not."),
 F("uncalled capital","the unrequested nominal amount on already issued shares","Issued nominal capital exceeds the amount requested so far.","Uncalled capital is identical to authorised but unissued capital.","These gaps concern different stages: issue first, then call."),
 F("reconciliation","checking that component amounts sum to the stated total","The pupil verifies that paid-up plus arrears equals called.","Adding unrelated capital-stage totals gives a valid financing total.","Overlapping stages must be reconciled, not counted as independent funds.")],practice[3],
 worked({},"A classroom record has {80} authorised shares, {50} issued shares, nominal value {1000}, a call of {600} per share and arrears of {2000} CFA francs. Reconcile the stages.",
 ["Authorised = {80*1000}; issued = {50*1000} CFA francs.","Called = {50*600}; paid-up = {50*600-2000} CFA francs.","Uncalled on the issue = {50*(1000-600)}. Check: {50*600}+{50*(1000-600)} = {50*1000}."],"Called {50*600} = paid-up {50*600-2000} + arrears {2000} CFA francs."),prereq=[6],questions=practice,figure=capital_record())

